-- Q611: Financial Statement Analysis [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The company is collecting its receivables at a faster rate than in prior periods","The company''s average collection period has increased from approximately 30 days to approximately 46 days","The company''s total revenue has decreased significantly over the two-year period","The company switched its accounting method from accrual basis to cash basis reporting"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Per AICPA ratio analysis principles, receivables turnover equals net credit sales divided by average accounts receivable. A decline from 12x to 8x means days sales outstanding increased from approximately 30 days (365/12) to approximately 46 days (365/8), indicating slower collections and weakening credit quality.
Wrong (A): A declining turnover ratio means slower collections, not faster.
Wrong (C): The stem states that sales remained relatively flat, so revenue did not decrease significantly.
