-- Q653: Risk Management and Economics [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The IRR ranking is correct because Beta''s 25% return exceeds Alpha''s 18%, making Beta the better project regardless of investment size","Both metrics always agree for mutually exclusive projects, so the conflicting data presented is mathematically impossible","The NPV ranking is more reliable because Alpha''s $450,000 NPV represents $130,000 more shareholder value than Beta''s $320,000, and IRR ignores scale differences","Neither metric is useful because NPV and IRR are only valid for evaluating independent projects, not mutually exclusive ones"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 360-10-35 capital budgeting principles, NPV is the more reliable criterion for mutually exclusive projects because it directly measures the dollar increase in shareholder wealth. Alpha creates $450,000 in value versus Beta''s $320,000. The conflict arises because IRR assumes reinvestment at the project''s own rate while NPV uses the more realistic WACC.
Wrong (A): A higher percentage return does not compensate for smaller absolute value creation when projects are mutually exclusive.
Wrong (B): NPV-IRR conflicts are common when projects have different scales or cash flow patterns.
Wrong (D): Both NPV and IRR are valid for evaluating mutually exclusive projects; NPV is simply more reliable when rankings conflict.$EXPL$
