  choices = $EXPL$["FastTrack recognizes the license fee at a point in time because the license transfers at signing, while GreenLeaf recognizes over time due to fewer ongoing obligations","Both franchisors recognize revenue at a point in time because franchise licenses always represent rights to use intellectual property at a specific point","FastTrack recognizes the fee over the 10-year term because its ongoing activities significantly affect the IP''s utility (access model), while GreenLeaf recognizes at grant date (use model)","Both franchisors recognize revenue over time because all franchise agreements involve multi-year terms that inherently require over-time revenue recognition"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 606-10-55-58 through 55-61, a license is recognized over time (access model) when the entity''s activities significantly affect the IP''s utility. FastTrack''s ongoing advertising, menu standards, and operational support meet these criteria, so revenue is recognized ratably over 10 years. GreenLeaf provides only static IP with no ongoing involvement, making it a right-to-use license recognized at grant.
