  choices = $EXPL$["Total compensation expense is $350,000 (10,000 * $35 intrinsic value at year-end) because ASC 718 requires mark-to-market adjustment for stock price changes","Total compensation expense is $0 because stock options are not considered compensatory until they are actually exercised by the employee","Total compensation expense is $450,000 (10,000 * $45 stock price at grant date) because the full stock price measures the cost of the award","Total compensation expense is $120,000 (10,000 * $12 grant-date fair value) recognized ratably over the vesting period under ASC 718"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 718, compensation cost for stock options is measured at the grant-date fair value ($12 per option) and is not subsequently remeasured. The total $120,000 expense is recognized ratably over the requisite service period. Subsequent stock appreciation benefits the employee but does not create additional compensation expense.
Wrong (A): ASC 718 specifically rejects mark-to-market treatment for equity-classified awards; grant-date fair value is fixed.
