-- Q694: Advanced Consolidations [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Kept at its original historical cost on the acquirer''s books with no adjustment","Remeasured to acquisition-date fair value with any resulting gain or loss in earnings","Written off entirely from the acquirer''s balance sheet as of the acquisition date","Adjusted only for cumulative equity method income recognized since original acquisition"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 805-10-25-10, when an acquirer obtains control in a step acquisition, the previously held equity interest must be remeasured to acquisition-date fair value with any gain or loss recognized in earnings. This ensures the entire combination is measured at fair value on the date control is achieved.
