-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The embedded derivative is clearly and closely related to the economic characteristics of the host contract","The host contract is already measured at fair value through earnings with changes recognized currently","The economic characteristics are not clearly and closely related to the host, and the hybrid instrument is not measured at fair value through earnings","The embedded derivative has a notional amount that exceeds a specified materiality threshold"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 815-15-25-1, an embedded derivative must be bifurcated when: (1) its economic characteristics are not clearly and closely related to the host, (2) the hybrid is not remeasured at fair value through earnings, and (3) a separate instrument with the same terms would be a derivative. All three must be met.
Wrong (A): Being clearly and closely related is a condition that exempts bifurcation, not one that requires it.
Wrong (B): If the host is already at fair value through earnings, bifurcation is unnecessary because fair value changes are already captured.
Wrong (D): Having a notional amount is part of the derivative definition but is not the condition triggering bifurcation.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 712;

-- Q713: Derivatives and Hedging [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The speculation exception for contracts entered into for trading purposes only","The normal purchases and normal sales scope exception under ASC 815","The embedded derivative exception for components within host contracts","The de minimis exception for contracts below a specified notional threshold"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 815-10-15-22, the normal purchases and normal sales (NPNS) scope exception permits entities to exclude contracts for physical delivery of nonfinancial assets used in normal business operations from derivative accounting. Bridgeport''s forward qualifies because it involves physical delivery of copper for regular production.
Wrong (A): There is no "speculation exception" in ASC 815; speculative contracts are subject to derivative accounting, not exempt from it.
Wrong (C): The embedded derivative exception relates to bifurcation of embedded features, not scope exclusion of standalone forward contracts.
Wrong (D): ASC 815 does not contain a de minimis exception based on notional amount.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 713;

-- Q719: Derivatives and Hedging [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Immediately reclassified to earnings in the period hedge accounting is discontinued","Left in OCI and reclassified to earnings when the hedged forecasted transaction affects earnings","Reversed against the carrying amount of the hedging instrument on the balance sheet","Written off directly to retained earnings as a prior-period adjustment"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 815-30-40-1, when hedge accounting is discontinued for a cash flow hedge, cumulative gains or losses in AOCI remain there and are reclassified into earnings when the forecasted transaction affects earnings. Amounts are not immediately reclassified unless the forecasted transaction is no longer probable of occurring.
Wrong (A): Immediate reclassification occurs only if the forecasted transaction is no longer probable, not upon mere discontinuance.
Wrong (C): The OCI balance is not reversed against the hedging instrument; it remains in accumulated OCI.
Wrong (D): The amounts are reclassified through earnings in future periods, not written off to retained earnings.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 719;

-- Q721: State and Local Government Reporting [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Fund-level recognizes $3 million and government-wide recognizes $2.6 million, because fund statements use the full levy while government-wide uses only cash collected","Both levels recognize $3 million because the full levy is measurable and collection timing is irrelevant under both measurement bases","Fund-level recognizes $2.85 million (collected plus amounts available within 60 days) while government-wide recognizes $3 million (full levy less estimated uncollectibles)","Fund-level recognizes $2.6 million on a cash basis while government-wide recognizes $2.85 million, because government-wide includes the 60-day availability window"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under modified accrual (GASB fund-level), revenue must be both measurable and available (collected within 60 days per GASB Statement No. 33). The $2.6M collected plus $250,000 within 60 days totals $2.85M; the $150,000 expected in October is deferred. Under full accrual (government-wide per GASB 34), revenue is recognized at the levy date, so the full $3M is recognized.
Wrong (A): This reverses the relationship; fund-level is more restrictive with the availability criterion, not less.
Wrong (B): Modified accrual explicitly requires availability, not just measurability.
Wrong (D): The 60-day window applies to fund-level modified accrual, not to government-wide full accrual.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 721;

-- Q723: State and Local Government Reporting [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Only governmental activities, excluding both business-type and fiduciary activities","Governmental and business-type activities, but not fiduciary activities","All fund types including fiduciary activities held in trust for external parties","Only business-type activities, excluding governmental and fiduciary activities"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB 34, government-wide statements report governmental activities and business-type activities but exclude fiduciary activities. Fiduciary resources are held in trust for others and are not available for the government''s own programs, so they appear only in fund-level fiduciary statements.
Wrong (A): Government-wide statements include both governmental and business-type activities, not just governmental.
Wrong (C): Fiduciary activities are excluded from government-wide statements; they have their own separate fund-level statements.
Wrong (D): Government-wide statements include governmental activities alongside business-type activities, not business-type alone.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 723;

-- Q724: State and Local Government Reporting [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Both statements report a $450,000 capital asset and depreciate it over its useful life under identical treatment per GASB 34","The governmental fund statements report a $450,000 expenditure reducing fund balance, while government-wide statements capitalize the asset and depreciate it over its life","The governmental fund statements capitalize the asset while the government-wide statements expense it, because government-wide uses a shorter-term measurement focus","Both statements report a $450,000 expenditure because governments cannot capitalize assets under any GASB standard"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB 34, governmental fund statements use the current financial resources measurement focus, so the $450,000 is reported as an expenditure reducing fund balance immediately. Government-wide statements use the economic resources measurement focus, so the asset is capitalized and depreciated over its useful life.
Wrong (A): GASB 34 specifically preserved different treatments at the fund level versus government-wide level.
Wrong (C): This reverses the treatment; fund statements expense while government-wide statements capitalize.
Wrong (D): GASB 34 requires capitalization of capital assets in government-wide statements.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 724;
